=== genuine design bug found and fixed before sealing ===
test_handoff_transfers_the_commitment_to_a_new_agent's own second-commit
step (by the new agent, after handoff) raised a real
ocor_runtime.errors.ConcurrencyConflict from the sealed
AtomicOutboxStore: commit()'s original idempotency_key was a fixed
f"commit:{task_id}" with no attempt counter, so a genuinely different
second commit (different agent_id) reused the identical idempotency
key as the first, and the sealed store correctly refused it as an
idempotency-key reuse for a different write request. Fixed by deriving
a real per-aggregate attempt counter from the store's own current
document version (store.get(aggregate_id)) for both assign() and
commit(), and using it in both idempotency_key and expected_version --
a correct, version-aware optimistic-concurrency write, not a
work-around.

